{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"braided-splurgy-toad","creation_channel":"python","description":"## Context\nThe generated configuration narrative says resolved configuration is exposed through an MCP configuration-transparency surface. Its adjacent heading also labels the topic as `MCP/CLI exposure`, although no MCP configuration tool exists. Both assertions originated in the accepted generator design on `consensual-ignored-ivorygull`.\n\n## Plan\n- In `scripts/gen_config_reference.py`, change the `Exposure (MCP/CLI exposure)` heading to `Exposure (CLI exposure)` and remove the `MCP config-transparency surface` clause so the paragraph describes only the implemented `rebar config` CLI view.\n- Retain accurate `rebar config` CLI exposure guidance.\n- Regenerate `docs/config-reference.md` and prove it is current with `python scripts/gen_config_reference.py --check`.\n- In `tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py`, rename the `REQUIRED_TOPICS` label from `mcp/cli exposure` to `cli exposure` while retaining positive coverage of the implemented CLI guidance.\n- In `tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py`, add an explicit negative assertion over the rendered configuration narrative that rejects each unsupported form: `MCP/CLI exposure`, `MCP config-transparency surface`, and `MCP configuration surface`.\n- Do not add an MCP tool or change configuration behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The generated heading is `Exposure (CLI exposure)` and the paragraph contains no MCP configuration-surface claim.\n- [x] Implemented CLI configuration inspection remains documented accurately.\n- [x] `python scripts/gen_config_reference.py --check` proves `docs/config-reference.md` is current after regeneration.\n- [x] Focused generator tests include the enumerated negative guard and fail on restoration of any removed MCP-exposure wording.\n- [x] Configuration runtime and MCP tool inventory are unchanged.","id":"73d5-6d4f-aa53-4b8c","parent_id":"f463-e20a-3e3b-4d29","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"F19A remove nonexistent MCP configuration exposure claim"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788223696447191001,"uuid":"44816111-a6df-4087-b284-2e1e574d051d"}